From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:07:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): web_extract always has a keyless provider

Extract resolution was capability-blind: autodetect returned searxng (SEARXNG_URL) for extract, then the dispatcher refused it as search-only, so every web_extract call failed on a default install. Autodetect, the shared web.backend and the registry walk now skip providers that lack the capability, and an unpinned extract ends on a built-in http-fetch provider (SSRF-guarded GET, manual redirects through the SSRF and website-policy gates, size cap, HTML to Markdown with the stdlib, PDFs through read_file's converter). Only an explicit web.extract_backend naming a search-only backend is an error, now one clear message that the startup config check also reports. web_extract's tool gate no longer depends on a web_search backend.
---
